# Cover details spoken as choices (docs/REPUTATION.md, "Borrowed kit"; docs/DIALOGUE.md, "Claims in
# someone else's kit"): a detail you really have (cover:<key>) counts at your next look with them for
# ten minutes, naming that very detail. One you don't have is a lie, caught at once. One claim line per
# speaker per life (claimed). The true answer, or leaving, costs nothing.

conv post.bastion.cover
for post:bastion
when kit:in_kit & !caught & !claimed
topic "Somebody here will vouch for me."
prio quest
voice bastion

node start
  say Will they. In Bastion kit and not on my board, you'd better have a name who'll stand for you, and stand next to you on the stockade list if it's wrong. Whose section are you?
  > @leader {cover:name} will stand for me. -> said   if cover:name   do cover:name
  > @dead {cover:dead} signed me on. -> said   if cover:dead   do cover:dead
  > @leave Forget it. -> hub

node said
  jump caught -> wrong
  say I'll remember that name, and I'll ask after it at the shift change. Now let's see if the rest of you matches it.
  > @claim One of yours. Let me through. -> passed | refused   check look bastion 2
  > @wait I'll wait till you've asked. -> hub

node passed
  say Go on. And if that name's wrong, it's both of you on the stockade list, and the name gets the worse end of it.
  do call:post_wave
  > @back1 It isn't wrong. One more thing. -> hub

node refused
  say No. The name's real enough, but you're not on its section and you never were. Hands on the barrier. That kit goes back to the stores.
  > @back2 Understood. -> hub

node wrong
  say Never heard that name on any roster I've read, and I've read every one that's come down this road. Hands on the barrier.
  > @back3 All right. Hands on the barrier. -> hub

conv post.redhand.cover
for post:redhand
when kit:in_kit & !caught & !claimed
topic "Ask anyone. The crews know me."
prio quest
voice redhand

node start
  say Go on, then. What does the crew call you, and who'd say so? A name's no good to me without somebody I know standing behind it.
  > @crew They call me {cover:crew}. -> said   if cover:crew   do cover:crew
  > @boss {cover:name} knows me. We go back. -> said   if cover:name   do cover:name
  > @leave Forget it. -> hub

node said
  jump caught -> wrong
  say Maybe. I've heard stupider names on better liars. Let's see if the rest of you matches it.
  > @claim One of yours. Wave me on. -> passed | caught2   check look redhand 2
  > @wait I'll just pay the toll. -> hub

node passed
  say Go on, then. And pay next time like everyone. Crew or no crew, the lorry doesn't move for free twice.
  do call:post_wave
  > @back1 Cheers. One more thing. -> hub

node caught2
  say No. Nobody on any road has ever called you that. Turn out your pockets, and let's see what else you've borrowed off the dead.
  > @back2 Fine. Pockets out. -> hub

node wrong
  say Nobody calls you that. Nobody ever has. I'd know: I'm the one who writes the names in the book.
  > @back3 Fine. You win. -> hub

conv named.halcyon.cover
for named:halcyon
when kit:in_kit & !caught & !claimed & cover:notebook
topic "I'm on the rota. Check my notebook."
prio quest
voice halcyon

node start
  say I don't have you on the rota, and I write the rota. Every one of us keeps a numbered notebook, and the lab keeps the numbers. Which one are you writing in?
  > @book Notebook {cover:notebook}, nights. -> said   do cover:notebook
  > @leave I'll go and check the rota. -> hub

node said
  jump caught -> wrong
  say Notebook {cover:notebook}. Yes, that number is one of ours, night shift. Carry on, then, quietly. The incubators don't like noise.
  > @back1 Thank you. -> hub

node wrong
  say There is no notebook with that number. There never was. I'm calling the guard, and I'm writing down that you tried.
  > @back2 Understood. -> hub

# What the kit remembers, without any claim: their reactions to the other kit kinds. Each line is a
# say? on what the kit says (the hub opens on the replies, so a plain line isn't shown).
conv named.bastion.kit_issued
for named:bastion
when kit:issued & tier:bastion<known
greet
voice bastion
daily

node start
  say? kit:issued :: You're still in our kit, and you're not on our board any more. Take it off before someone asks why, and before the stores want it back with a signature.

conv named.bastion.kit_dead
for named:bastion
when kit:dead_mans & !passing
greet
voice bastion
daily

node start
  say? kit:dead_mans :: That's issue kit with the name tape picked off. We know whose tape that was. The tag's on our nail, and that jacket should have gone in the ground.

conv named.bastion.kit_turned
for named:bastion
when kit:off_turned
greet
voice bastion
daily

node start
  say? kit:off_turned :: That jacket's been on one of the turned. You can smell it from here. Burn it, don't wash it, and don't wear it anywhere near our wire.

conv named.bastion.kit_signed
for named:bastion
when kit:signed_other & !passing
greet
voice bastion
daily

node start
  say? kit:signed_other :: That set's signed out of our stores, and not to you. The quartermaster keeps a book, and that number's in it beside someone else's name.
